From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bron Gondwana <brong@fastmailteam.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 22:44:10 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] Add DKIM2 Message-Instance headers

Implement the Message-Instance header of draft-ietf-dkim-dkim2-spec-09,
so that a DKIM2 verifier can undo what a list changed and re-verify the
signatures of earlier hops.  Mailman adds the instances; the MTA signs.

With the new [mta] message_instance setting on (off by default):

- The LMTP runner records the digests of the post as received, the
  length and line count of its body and where it has "From " lines,
  checks any Message-Instance it came with, and starts the header log.
  From then on Message also marks any part whose payload changes.

- The message-instance-ingress handler takes its snapshot from that
  record.  A signed post's instances are left alone; an unsigned post
  leaves with a single m=1.

- Decoration never re-encodes a post, so it can be found again.

- At delivery, after decoration, personalization and ARC signing, a
  changed message gets m=N+1, with header and body Recipes back to the
  snapshot, each checked against its digest.  The body Recipe comes from
  where decoration put the post, found by flattening only what
  decoration added, without scanning the message.

- From becomes the list's posting address whenever the list changes or
  originates a post.  Whether the body will change is decided without
  serializing it.

- Each instance comes with an X-DKIM2-Info debugging header.

src/mailman/handlers/docs/message-instance.rst describes the design.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
